{"exhaustive":{"nbHits":false,"typo":false},"exhaustiveNbHits":false,"exhaustiveTypo":false,"hits":[{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["mrr"],"value":"<em>mar</em>ko-projects"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Free daily logic puzzles without Ads.\nCheck it out: gridmino.com<p>My site offers puzzles where some of them are a new take on already established classics like Minesweeper, Kakuro, or Masyu. For example, my Minesweeper is called Dicesweep, where you need to place dice beside numbers while also matching the row and column rules.<p>Another interesting one is Kakumino. It's like Kakuro, but you place dominoes instead of numbers.<p>There are a bunch of them, so there's something for everyone's taste.<p>Check it out: gridmino.com"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Show HN: Take a break, play some puzzles"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://gridmino.com/"}},"_tags":["story","author_marko-projects","story_50335122","show_hn"],"author":"marko-projects","created_at":"2026-11-02T10:34:38Z","created_at_i":1793615678,"num_comments":0,"objectID":"50335122","points":1,"story_id":50335122,"story_text":"Free daily logic puzzles without Ads.\nCheck it out: gridmino.com<p>My site offers puzzles where some of them are a new take on already established classics like Minesweeper, Kakuro, or Masyu. For example, my Minesweeper is called Dicesweep, where you need to place dice beside numbers while also matching the row and column rules.<p>Another interesting one is Kakumino. It&#x27;s like Kakuro, but you place dominoes instead of numbers.<p>There are a bunch of them, so there&#x27;s something for everyone&#x27;s taste.<p>Check it out: gridmino.com","title":"Show HN: Take a break, play some puzzles","updated_at":"2026-11-02T10:35:41Z","url":"https://gridmino.com/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"jongjong"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["mrr"],"value":"IMO, the real reason they were laid off is because our economic system is broken. It's wealth concentration for those in the center of the scheme and deprivation for those in the periphery.<p>Rapid technological improvement is just a convenient justification for letting people go. It sounds a lot better than the real explanation &quot;The system is broken and we need to keep optimizing money flows to sustain the scheme to prevent hyperinflation.&quot; The system destroys value faster than technology can create it; which is quite an impressive feat because technology opens up massive capabilities but look at reality; AI is being massively misallocated.<p><em>Mar</em>k my words; the business model for AI, if the current trends continue, isn't going to be about &quot;robots making everyone's lives better&quot;; it's going to be about &quot;AI agents which patch vulnerabilities that AI agents themselves created.&quot;<p>This is the reality we're heading into. No amount of incredible technology is going to solve that problem if it follows the rules of the current economic system. That's what the incentives lead to."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"OccupySaaS"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://occupysaas.com/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_jongjong","story_50331402"],"author":"jongjong","comment_text":"IMO, the real reason they were laid off is because our economic system is broken. It&#x27;s wealth concentration for those in the center of the scheme and deprivation for those in the periphery.<p>Rapid technological improvement is just a convenient justification for letting people go. It sounds a lot better than the real explanation &quot;The system is broken and we need to keep optimizing money flows to sustain the scheme to prevent hyperinflation.&quot; The system destroys value faster than technology can create it; which is quite an impressive feat because technology opens up massive capabilities but look at reality; AI is being massively misallocated.<p>Mark my words; the business model for AI, if the current trends continue, isn&#x27;t going to be about &quot;robots making everyone&#x27;s lives better&quot;; it&#x27;s going to be about &quot;AI agents which patch vulnerabilities that AI agents themselves created.&quot;<p>This is the reality we&#x27;re heading into. No amount of incredible technology is going to solve that problem if it follows the rules of the current economic system. That&#x27;s what the incentives lead to.","created_at":"2026-11-02T10:33:36Z","created_at_i":1793615616,"objectID":"50335118","parent_id":50334779,"story_id":50331402,"story_title":"OccupySaaS","story_url":"https://occupysaas.com/","updated_at":"2026-11-02T10:35:41Z"}],"hitsPerPage":2,"nbHits":47830,"nbPages":500,"page":0,"params":"query=MRR&tags=%28comment%2Cshow_hn%29&hitsPerPage=2&page=0&numericFilters=created_at_i%3E%3D1791024825%2Ccreated_at_i%3C%3D1793616825&advancedSyntax=true&analyticsTags=backend","processingTimeMS":38,"processingTimingsMS":{"_request":{"queue":6,"roundTrip":17},"fetch":{"query":11,"scanning":25,"total":37},"total":38},"query":"MRR","serverTimeMS":45}
